LINES = ['In 1892, this country lived the same day twice.', "American traders convinced Samoa's king to switch to the American date, so Monday, July fourth, happened two times.", 'But over a century later, its business had shifted to New Zealand, Australia and Asia, and Samoa was a full day behind them.', 'So in 2011, it jumped back across the date line and deleted Friday, December thirtieth.', 'People went to bed on Thursday and woke up on Saturday.', 'And if your birthday was that Friday? Sorry. Business first.']
